      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The reason to hear this is the saxophone conversation, not tribute prestige. Aldana, Weldon, Lewis and Chung bring different generations and different relationships to time, tone and melodic development into the same front line, with Allison directing a rhythm section built to leave room for improvisation. Rollins' language becomes a live point of departure rather than a museum object.",
