      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This is more than a Gilberto Gil songbook night. Wilmer has built a new large-ensemble language around the material, using Brazilian rhythmic cells, extended horn color and Salmaso's unusually precise phrasing to move the songs between MPB memory and contemporary jazz orchestration. Hearing the freshly released project opened up across a working big ensemble is exactly the kind of cultural translation that earns a place on RADAR.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for one of the six sets if a New York trip overlaps September 11-13. It can anchor a strong evening in the city and pairs naturally with other jazz around the weekend, while three nights give enough flexibility that the trip does not need to revolve around a single scarce performance.",
